WEBVTT

00:04.880 --> 00:08.236
Well, that was just lovely.

00:08.960 --> 00:10.439
I do aim to please.

00:10.600 --> 00:14.195
And after last time,
I appreciate the aiming.

00:15.040 --> 00:18.715
Hey, we made good time.
I can let the babysitter go early.

00:18.880 --> 00:20.518
The key is efficient foreplay.

00:20.680 --> 00:25.470
Minimal attention to each breast
before I meander to your dander.

00:27.040 --> 00:29.031
- Spoon?
- Sure.

00:36.320 --> 00:38.311
And switch.

00:45.000 --> 00:47.195
- That was fun.
- It always is.

00:47.360 --> 00:49.191
Okay, well, drive safe.

00:49.360 --> 00:51.510
- I always do.
- I know, I'm just a worrier.

00:51.680 --> 00:53.272
I know you are.

00:53.640 --> 00:55.517
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

00:59.280 --> 01:01.589
I get more tongue from my butcher.

01:06.320 --> 01:08.959
I'm sorry, did you consider
making your presence known?

01:09.120 --> 01:10.917
Clear your throat, maybe a little cough?

01:11.080 --> 01:14.595
I wanted to vomit, but I was
afraid it might break the mood.

01:14.760 --> 01:17.752
Hey, hey. Postcoital kissing
is always more platonic.

01:17.920 --> 01:20.150
- Is it?
- Yes, because, well...

01:20.320 --> 01:22.390
...we both know
where our mouths have been.

01:22.640 --> 01:23.629
I see.

01:23.800 --> 01:26.360
But in the bedroom,
there was a lot of saliva...

01:26.520 --> 01:28.954
...and heat, and friction,
believe you me.

01:29.280 --> 01:32.192
- Really?
- Yes, really.

01:35.040 --> 01:37.031
It may not have been
crazy, hot, monkey sex...

01:37.200 --> 01:38.872
...like when we first started dating.

01:39.040 --> 01:43.477
But it was very much in the
general category of jungle humping.

01:44.240 --> 01:46.276
- Jungle humping?
- Yes.

01:46.440 --> 01:47.873
Maybe not tree swinging...

01:48.040 --> 01:51.350
...but certainly canoodling
on some low-hanging branches.

01:51.520 --> 01:53.556
You poor bastard.

01:53.720 --> 01:55.711
Don't you dare feel sorry for me.

01:55.880 --> 01:58.440
This is what an adult relationship
looks like, Charlie.

01:58.600 --> 02:01.273
People get comfortable with each other
and develop a routine.

02:01.440 --> 02:03.635
And if it's not always fireworks
and explosions...

02:03.800 --> 02:07.588
...well, that's a reasonable trade
for a warm, collegial partnership.

02:09.720 --> 02:12.393
You poor, poor bastard.

02:12.680 --> 02:14.671
This conversation is over.

02:14.840 --> 02:15.989
If only.

02:18.560 --> 02:20.391
Okay, it's boring. It's suffocating.

02:20.560 --> 02:22.994
It's a deathwatch,
but what choice do I have, Charlie?

02:23.160 --> 02:24.434
Pretend I'm you? I'm not you.

02:24.600 --> 02:27.398
I'm monogamous, settle-down guy
who hangs onto a relationship...

02:27.560 --> 02:30.870
...until I'm looking at divorce papers
or the pointy end of a steak knife.

02:31.040 --> 02:32.519
Oh, that's a load of crap.

02:32.680 --> 02:36.639
You're afraid if you let go of these
broads you're never gonna get laid again.

02:36.800 --> 02:39.075
Didn't I just say that?

02:50.520 --> 02:52.750
Boxing sucks.

02:53.160 --> 02:55.799
As always,
you're entitled to your stupid opinion.

02:58.360 --> 03:00.999
Why are you making it personal?
I didn't make it personal.

03:02.760 --> 03:04.512
In Ultimate Fighting, they kick, elbow.

03:04.680 --> 03:06.989
They get a guy down
and smash his head in the floor.

03:07.160 --> 03:09.879
These guys just dance around
and barely hit each other.

03:10.040 --> 03:11.712
Okay, okay, listen to me.

03:11.880 --> 03:13.711
Boxing is a science.

03:13.880 --> 03:15.677
Boxers don't just
whale on each other...

03:15.840 --> 03:18.832
...they strategize, feel each other out,
wait for an opening.

03:21.400 --> 03:22.879
Gay.

03:25.240 --> 03:27.435
And what's with the little pillows
on their hands?

03:27.600 --> 03:30.034
Even if they hit each other,
it wouldn't hurt.

03:34.440 --> 03:35.429
Oh, does that hurt?

03:35.600 --> 03:37.636
- Yeah.
- Good.

03:38.840 --> 03:41.070
- Hey, what are you doing?
- Uncle Charlie hit me.

03:41.240 --> 03:42.593
Good.

03:43.840 --> 03:45.876
- Where have you been?
- I'll tell you later.

03:46.040 --> 03:48.998
Tell him now, I got better things to do.

03:50.800 --> 03:52.870
You promised he'd grow on me.

03:53.400 --> 03:54.992
I lied.

03:56.120 --> 03:59.078
- So where were you?
- Well, I thought about what you said...

03:59.240 --> 04:02.516
...and I went over to Donna's house
to break up with her.

04:02.920 --> 04:05.150
- I'm proud of you.
- Thanks.

04:06.160 --> 04:08.594
I'm gonna meet her parents
next weekend.

04:09.640 --> 04:11.870
- But you just said...
- I know, but I couldn't do it.

04:12.040 --> 04:14.952
I'm not capable
of rejecting another human being.

04:15.240 --> 04:18.835
Wow, I'd think after all these years,
you'd wanna get even.

04:20.640 --> 04:21.993
I am in trouble here, Charlie.

04:22.160 --> 04:24.674
How do I get out of a stagnant,
joyless relationship?

04:25.080 --> 04:28.072
If I knew how to do that,
you wouldn't still be living here.

04:32.280 --> 04:34.589
Okay, first...

04:35.600 --> 04:38.751
...you gotta get your mind right.
- How do I do that?

04:38.920 --> 04:41.992
Close your eyes
and imagine a parallel world...

04:42.160 --> 04:45.470
...where there's an Alan Harper
exactly like you.

04:45.640 --> 04:48.916
Except he's got a set of balls.

04:52.880 --> 04:56.111
- You wanna help me here or not?
- Hey, it's gotta be fun for me too.

04:58.720 --> 05:01.075
Fine. We'll just assume
that your mind is right.

05:02.640 --> 05:06.428
Now, before you do the actual dumping,
there's a few things you gotta consider.

05:06.600 --> 05:08.113
Like what?

05:08.280 --> 05:11.636
Does she have embarrassing photographs
that could wind up on the Internet...

05:11.800 --> 05:12.915
...if she takes it badly?

05:13.080 --> 05:14.752
I'm not sure.

05:15.080 --> 05:16.274
What do you mean?

05:16.440 --> 05:19.432
Well, there's one of me naked,
but I'm wearing a mask and a cape.

05:19.600 --> 05:23.309
- I thought the sex was mundane.
- Sadly, it still was.

05:24.640 --> 05:26.278
Whatever, she can't use the picture.

05:26.440 --> 05:28.431
Does she have your
credit card information?

05:28.600 --> 05:30.795
- No.
- Don't answer so quickly.

05:31.400 --> 05:35.188
I once handed a date my Visa
so she could pump gas for me...

05:35.560 --> 05:37.835
...and on my next statement
there were charges...

05:38.000 --> 05:39.831
...for a boob job and a PlayStation 3.

05:40.800 --> 05:43.314
And I never got to play
with either one of them.

05:45.080 --> 05:46.911
You made your date pump gas?

05:47.320 --> 05:49.675
I liked the song that was on the radio.

05:50.480 --> 05:53.790
But back to the topic at hand.
Does she own any chick weapons?

05:53.960 --> 05:55.154
Chick weapons?

05:55.320 --> 05:58.756
You know, little guns, Tasers,
pepper spray.

05:58.920 --> 06:01.070
Well, there's a baseball bat
by her front door...

06:01.240 --> 06:03.231
...but I think that's for intruders.

06:03.400 --> 06:06.198
Yeah, I've made that mistake too.

06:08.600 --> 06:12.559
Okay. Let's talk about
the where, when and how.

06:13.280 --> 06:16.829
Where: Always break up in public place.
That way you avoid having a scene.

06:17.000 --> 06:18.228
- That makes sense.
- When:

06:18.400 --> 06:21.472
Before the desert menu comes out.
Otherwise, you can find yourself...

06:21.640 --> 06:24.791
...with a lap full of hot coffee,
which is not as fun as it sounds.

06:24.960 --> 06:26.029
That doesn't sound fun.

06:26.200 --> 06:28.668
It sounds fun if you're
wearing a couple of doughnuts.

06:33.640 --> 06:35.153
Moving on to how.

06:37.080 --> 06:38.513
What you wanna convey...

06:38.680 --> 06:42.195
...is your undying affection and
gratitude for your time spent together...

06:42.360 --> 06:45.636
...coupled with your need for space
to find out who you really are.

06:45.800 --> 06:47.472
- But that's crap.
- It's all crap.

06:47.640 --> 06:49.631
You know it, she knows it,
everybody knows it.

06:50.040 --> 06:51.234
All we're trying to do...

06:51.400 --> 06:54.039
...is keep her from taking batting
practice on your kidneys.

06:54.200 --> 06:55.599
Why would she go for my kidneys?

06:55.760 --> 06:58.194
Because you'll be running away
covering your head.

06:58.360 --> 07:02.672
Okay, okay. So I take her to dinner,
and then before the coffee comes...

07:02.840 --> 07:05.400
...I tell her that
while I have strong feelings for her...

07:05.560 --> 07:07.471
...I need time to find out
who I really am.

07:07.880 --> 07:08.915
Excellent.

07:09.080 --> 07:12.516
Maybe I could throw in some stuff about
how I'm still reeling from my divorce.

07:12.680 --> 07:15.114
Don't improvise.
You don't have the chops for it.

07:16.120 --> 07:17.838
- Sorry.
- No problem.

07:18.000 --> 07:21.470
- I do appreciate the advice.
- You're very welcome.

07:29.320 --> 07:31.709
A mask and a cape,
and the sex was boring?

07:32.120 --> 07:35.396
What can I say?
She still knew it was me.

07:42.040 --> 07:43.393
How do I look?

07:44.280 --> 07:46.430
What difference does it make?
You're breaking up.

07:46.600 --> 07:49.637
I don't want my clothes to say
"come hither."

07:49.800 --> 07:53.634
Don't worry. As always, they say
"your regular teacher is sick."

07:56.280 --> 07:58.271
- Are we clear on everything I told you?
- Yes.

07:58.440 --> 08:01.591
I'm gonna go to her house, pick her up,
take her to the restaurant...

08:02.480 --> 08:05.199
Pick her up?
You're supposed to meet her there.

08:05.360 --> 08:07.635
- Why?
- What do you mean, why?

08:07.800 --> 08:10.394
You're gonna break up with her
and then drive her home?

08:11.320 --> 08:13.788
You'll need the Jaws of Life
to get her out of your car.

08:13.960 --> 08:17.350
- You didn't say anything about that.
- It's common sense.

08:17.520 --> 08:21.593
Do you know why Custer and Sitting Bull
didn't share a pony to Little Bighorn?

08:21.880 --> 08:23.871
They knew
there were gonna be hurt feelings...

08:24.040 --> 08:26.270
...and the ride home
would be awkward.

08:27.000 --> 08:30.197
- I'm just gonna call her and reschedule.
- No, no, no, you're not.

08:30.360 --> 08:31.429
Here's what you do.

08:31.600 --> 08:33.716
You're gonna pick her up,
have a nice dinner...

08:33.880 --> 08:35.950
...drive her home
and walk her to her door.

08:36.120 --> 08:38.680
- What if she asks me in?
- No, never go inside.

08:40.200 --> 08:42.668
Everything in her house
is a potential weapon.

08:43.360 --> 08:44.429
Everything?

08:44.600 --> 08:47.114
I was once blinded for two days
by potpourri.

08:49.840 --> 08:54.231
So you just walk her to her door...

08:54.400 --> 08:56.038
...take her by the hand...

08:56.200 --> 08:58.350
...and tell her
that you've had wonderful times...

08:58.520 --> 09:00.590
...and those are the memories
you will cherish.

09:00.760 --> 09:03.354
You know, we did have
wonderful times.

09:03.520 --> 09:07.638
Hiking in Catalina,
go-carting in Oxnard...

09:07.920 --> 09:09.876
...Oktoberfest in Rosemead.

09:11.320 --> 09:14.278
What a day that was.
Sharing bratwurst and sauerkraut...

09:14.440 --> 09:17.352
...while listening
to the battle of the oompah bands.

09:18.040 --> 09:19.951
Oh, God.
Do you think I'm making a mistake?

09:20.120 --> 09:24.591
No, no, no. The mind plays tricks on us.
It only remembers the good times.

09:24.760 --> 09:27.638
Or in your case,
the creepy, pathetic times.

09:28.320 --> 09:30.788
- But I still...
- Don't worry, Alan.

09:30.960 --> 09:33.394
There'll be other broads
to share your bratwurst with.

09:34.920 --> 09:36.558
You're right, I have to do this.

09:39.000 --> 09:42.037
But wait, what...?
What if she starts crying?

09:42.200 --> 09:46.034
You hold her in your arms, whisper
that this is best for both of you...

09:46.200 --> 09:48.430
...then turn around
and walk away like a man.

09:49.560 --> 09:53.553
Unless you hear a distinct
metallic click, then zigzag and roll.

10:05.640 --> 10:07.232
Hi. Come on in.

10:08.880 --> 10:11.155
That's okay, I'm kind of hungry.
Let's just go.

10:11.320 --> 10:13.834
Well, actually,
I thought we could stay in tonight.

10:14.360 --> 10:16.316
- Really?
- I'm making fondue.

10:16.480 --> 10:19.313
- Come on.
- Oh, goody.

10:19.480 --> 10:21.675
Hot cheese and long, sharp forks.

10:43.760 --> 10:46.433
This movie is stupid.

10:47.720 --> 10:49.517
This movie is a classic.

10:49.680 --> 10:53.195
It's been 40 minutes and we
haven't even seen the shark yet.

10:53.360 --> 10:57.114
That's because they're building suspense,
letting you use your imagination.

10:57.280 --> 11:00.750
You know what I'm imagining?
A better movie.

11:01.480 --> 11:04.517
- It's a classic, Jake.
- I'll tell you what's a classic.

11:04.680 --> 11:05.954
&lt;i>Snakes on a Plane.&lt;/i>

11:06.520 --> 11:09.398
First, you're in an airplane,
which is scary to begin with...

11:09.560 --> 11:11.357
...and then it's all filled with snakes.

11:11.520 --> 11:12.953
And they're everywhere.

11:13.120 --> 11:16.556
They're in the overhead compartments,
in the bathrooms, in the vomit bags.

11:18.200 --> 11:20.760
You need to throw up,
open the bag, snake.

11:21.200 --> 11:23.077
Sounds gripping.

11:23.240 --> 11:24.958
Snake.

11:31.560 --> 11:33.039
Snake.

11:34.840 --> 11:37.752
- That's it. We're out of here.
- Where are we going?

11:37.920 --> 11:41.117
Someplace public, where killing you
would get me in trouble.

11:41.280 --> 11:42.713
Fine.

11:42.880 --> 11:44.438
Snake.

11:46.000 --> 11:47.797
- Great fondue, Donna.
- Glad you liked it.

11:47.960 --> 11:50.599
Oh, don't forget
to put away the little forks.

11:50.880 --> 11:53.792
Thanks. Be right back.

12:00.320 --> 12:02.197
Oh, good Lord.

12:05.800 --> 12:07.677
We've had wonderful times together,
Donna.

12:07.840 --> 12:10.354
And those are memories
I will always cherish.

12:10.520 --> 12:12.476
- What?
- Nothing.

12:16.200 --> 12:17.997
The potpourri.

12:30.440 --> 12:31.668
I made coffee.

12:32.040 --> 12:34.315
- Hot coffee?
- Well, yeah.

12:34.800 --> 12:36.358
Of course it's hot.

12:38.280 --> 12:41.670
Oh, my. That is potentially scalding.

12:41.840 --> 12:45.037
- Blow on it, silly.
- Yes, blowing.

12:46.240 --> 12:47.593
You blow too.

12:49.640 --> 12:53.474
So listen, Donna, there's something
we really need to talk about.

12:53.640 --> 12:57.155
- What's that?
- Well, I was wondering.

12:57.720 --> 13:01.190
Are you completely happy
in this relationship?

13:01.360 --> 13:04.432
- Oh, good, then it's not just me.
- What do you mean?

13:04.600 --> 13:06.909
Well, I enjoy spending time with you...

13:07.080 --> 13:10.311
...but, honey, I kind of feel
like we're getting a little stale.

13:10.480 --> 13:12.630
Really? I thought it was going great.

13:12.800 --> 13:17.476
Come on, Alan. Our sex life is pathetic.
We're just going through the motions.

13:17.640 --> 13:20.757
Well, now, hold on.
Those motions are tried and true.

13:20.920 --> 13:23.753
Call it whatever you want.
Tried and true, dull and listless.

13:23.920 --> 13:25.990
I wanna call it tried and true.

13:26.160 --> 13:29.596
All I know is every time we get in bed,
it's the same old thing.

13:29.760 --> 13:32.274
The same old thing?
What about the mask and cape?

13:32.680 --> 13:35.911
It was the same old thing
in a mask and cape.

13:36.080 --> 13:37.559
Please don't take it personally.

13:37.720 --> 13:39.870
Oh, no. How can I possibly
take it personally?

13:40.040 --> 13:42.952
- You're just telling me I'm a lousy lay.
- No, I didn't mean lousy.

13:43.120 --> 13:46.874
I meant uninspired, lackluster,
predictable.

13:47.040 --> 13:50.510
- Okay.
- Tedious, mind-numbing, boring...

13:50.680 --> 13:52.796
All right, that's it.
Come upstairs with me.

13:52.960 --> 13:55.793
I will show you tedious,
mind-numbing and boring.

13:56.280 --> 13:57.508
Oh, God. I'm sorry.

13:57.680 --> 13:59.671
- Hot, hot, hot.
- What can I do?

13:59.840 --> 14:02.115
I don't know, just do something.

14:12.160 --> 14:14.549
How can you say this is boring?

14:16.120 --> 14:18.475
Wait till you try this.
It's the best pizza in town.

14:18.640 --> 14:21.074
- Says who?
- They put a flyer on Mom's windshield.

14:21.240 --> 14:22.719
It said "best pizza in town."

14:23.240 --> 14:25.629
Jake, let me give you
a little culinary advice.

14:25.800 --> 14:27.916
Any restaurant
that advertises on windshields...

14:28.080 --> 14:32.073
...and has a guy dressed as a hoagie
is probably not the best in town.

14:32.240 --> 14:35.152
He wasn't a hoagie, he was a calzone.

14:41.680 --> 14:43.352
- Amazing.
- What?

14:43.520 --> 14:46.080
How can a kid with such
lousy taste in pizza and movies...

14:46.240 --> 14:48.151
...have such good taste in girls?

14:49.640 --> 14:51.949
- She is kind of cute.
- Why don't you go talk to her?

14:52.120 --> 14:53.348
I don't know what to say.

14:53.520 --> 14:56.239
That's never stopped you
from running your mouth before.

14:58.080 --> 15:00.833
- What about her mom?
- Just stick with the daughter for now.

15:01.000 --> 15:03.195
- No, I mean...
- I know what you mean.

15:03.360 --> 15:06.113
Tell you what. I'll be your wingman.

15:06.280 --> 15:08.555
I'll go over
and engage the mom in conversation.

15:08.720 --> 15:11.154
Then after I grease the wheels,
I'll give you a signal.

15:11.320 --> 15:13.117
You saunter over and work your magic.

15:13.280 --> 15:15.510
- Saunter?
- Walk.

15:15.680 --> 15:18.353
Well, then just say walk.
You don't have to make up words.

15:21.000 --> 15:22.797
Wait, what's the signal?

15:23.280 --> 15:26.636
- I don't know, I'll give you a thumbs up.
- That's not much of a signal.

15:26.800 --> 15:29.758
All right, how about I just wave my arms
and say, "Yo, dumb-ass."

15:30.320 --> 15:32.231
Let's go with the thumb.

15:37.040 --> 15:39.270
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

15:39.440 --> 15:42.955
I'm sorry to interrupt your dinner, but
I'm sitting over there with my nephew...

15:43.120 --> 15:45.315
- Now?
- No, not now.

15:46.080 --> 15:47.832
- Dumb-ass.
- Now?

15:49.280 --> 15:50.998
No.

15:51.160 --> 15:53.754
Anyway, he's taken a bit of a shine
to your daughter...

15:53.920 --> 15:57.276
...and it would mean the world to him
if he could come over and meet her.

15:57.760 --> 16:00.558
That's very sweet,
and I don't wanna seem impolite...

16:00.720 --> 16:03.029
...but this is our one-on-one time.

16:03.200 --> 16:06.510
I understand. You should have that.
We're only talking a couple of minutes.

16:06.680 --> 16:09.478
- Enough time to put a smile on a boy's...
- Now?

16:10.200 --> 16:11.872
No.

16:13.360 --> 16:17.399
Look, I appreciate you coming over,
but I think we'll pass.

16:17.560 --> 16:20.358
Fine. Sorry to bother you.

16:20.920 --> 16:22.672
Real smooth.

16:25.720 --> 16:27.597
Okay, you really gotta
help me out here.

16:27.760 --> 16:31.070
- Sir, I'm having dinner with my daughter.
- And I am here with my nephew.

16:31.240 --> 16:33.071
They'd rather be sitting and talking...

16:33.240 --> 16:35.674
...than hanging out
with a couple of old farts like us.

16:36.200 --> 16:39.636
- What did you call me?
- No, no, no. Not you, us.

16:39.800 --> 16:41.028
I was being funny.

16:42.240 --> 16:44.708
I don't think you're funny at all.

16:44.880 --> 16:48.759
Well, clearly you don't know me.
I'm Charlie.

16:48.920 --> 16:52.515
Yes, well, Charlie,
I've asked you to leave us alone.

16:52.680 --> 16:55.558
- I understand, and I will, but...
- Honey, get me a refill.

16:56.160 --> 16:57.639
Yo, dumb-ass. Go get a refill.

16:57.800 --> 16:59.199
- Now?
- Yes, now.

17:01.320 --> 17:03.151
My brother's kid's not real...

17:07.880 --> 17:11.714
- I warned you.
- God, it's worse than the potpourri.

17:15.080 --> 17:16.479
I see you like the diet cola.

17:16.640 --> 17:19.393
If I may say so,
you don't need to watch your weight.

17:23.880 --> 17:27.190
- Here you go. Clean and dry.
- Thank you, thank you.

17:27.360 --> 17:30.477
- Are you all right?
- Oh, yeah. Little Alan's fine.

17:30.640 --> 17:32.870
The twins got the worst of it.

17:33.280 --> 17:34.599
Good, good.

17:35.000 --> 17:38.549
Listen, Donna. You were right.

17:38.720 --> 17:41.314
- This relationship is over.
- Over?

17:41.480 --> 17:44.074
Well, what else is there to do
besides call it quits?

17:44.240 --> 17:47.118
Oh, I thought maybe
we could take it to the next level.

17:47.880 --> 17:48.869
Next level?

17:49.040 --> 17:51.190
What's beyond mind-numbing,
tedious and boring?

17:52.360 --> 17:54.828
I'll tell you what's beyond it. Death.

17:55.120 --> 17:56.758
No, thank you. Already been married.

17:56.920 --> 17:58.672
- But, Alan...
- I'm sorry, but it's just...

17:58.840 --> 18:00.671
It's time we faced the truth. L...

18:00.840 --> 18:02.831
I have no romantic feelings
for you anymore.

18:03.400 --> 18:05.868
- None?
- None at all.

18:08.680 --> 18:09.795
Come on, Donna.

18:09.960 --> 18:11.951
Crying doesn't solve anything.
Believe me.

18:12.120 --> 18:14.918
It's better to end this now
while we're still friends.

18:20.800 --> 18:23.758
- Goodbye, my friend.
- Oh, just get out.

18:40.040 --> 18:43.191
- What are you doing?
- Nothing.

18:44.680 --> 18:47.752
- Oh, hi. You must be Alan.
- Yes.

18:48.480 --> 18:51.392
Forget it, Georgia.
It's not gonna happen.

18:57.640 --> 18:59.232
What's not gonna happen?

18:59.400 --> 19:03.837
I thought I could spice up our
relationship with a three-way.

19:06.880 --> 19:08.393
A three-way?

19:08.560 --> 19:12.519
But I didn't realize you had
no romantic feelings for me at all.

19:13.320 --> 19:15.038
Now, hang on.

19:16.640 --> 19:18.835
I think you may have misinterpreted
my remarks.

19:19.000 --> 19:21.434
Oh, honey. I'm here for you.

19:21.600 --> 19:24.512
Now, see, you really need to be
more clear about what you meant...

19:24.680 --> 19:26.272
...by taking it to the next level.

19:26.440 --> 19:28.715
See, I'm fine with this.

19:29.120 --> 19:32.908
- This could help.
- Oh, go to hell.

19:57.320 --> 19:58.878
Was the friend good-Iooking?

19:59.440 --> 20:01.795
Spectacular.

20:03.240 --> 20:06.437
Sounds like you blew what could have
been the best night of your life.

20:06.600 --> 20:10.115
The best night? No, no.
That was the night Jake was born.

20:10.480 --> 20:13.199
You have a three-way
the night Jake was born?

20:13.720 --> 20:16.393
Okay, I blew the best night of my life.

20:16.800 --> 20:19.598
Well, don't worry. You'll have
another opportunity someday.

20:19.760 --> 20:22.593
- How do you figure?
- You may have to wait a few decades.

20:22.760 --> 20:27.993
But I hear the ratio of gals to geezers
in senior-living facilities is two-to-one.

20:29.000 --> 20:32.515
Imagine the progress they'll have made
in boner pills by that time.

20:34.760 --> 20:36.716
Are you staring at me?

20:37.880 --> 20:40.952
Because it feels like
you're staring at me.

21:05.200 --> 21:07.191
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

21:07.360 --> 21:09.351
[ENGLISH]
